  1   # lensd specification
  2
  3   What lensd guarantees, as definitions (`**Def $Name (title).**`) and invariants
  4   (`**$Name (title).**`). Normative statements use
  5   MUST. Every invariant names what checks it: a TLA+ model in spec/tla/ (each with a
      deliberately broken
  6   "mutant" that TLC must reject), a Go test, or a runtime check. Go tests cite what they check
      with a
  7   comment directly above the test:
  8
  9       // Spec: $Frame.Timing §1 "quoted text from this file"
 10
 11   and code may cite the invariant it enforces (`// $Sdk.NvrAgrees: ...`). A spec change and the
      matching test
 12   or model change go in the same commit. Values marked (code: …) also exist as constants;
      changing one
 13   means changing the other. Liveness is stated as bounded-time rules on lensd's own clock
      ($Time.Elapsed),
 14   not as TLA+ liveness properties. Trace verification (checking runtime traces against the
      models) is out
 15   of scope.
 16
 17   ## Context (for readers without the code)
 18
 19   lensd is a Go web gateway for two NVRs at one site. It relays live RTSP from the NVR (one
 20   session per camera shared by all viewers), plays recordings through a vendor SDK helper
